{
  "name": "02 - Processing / Validate Transaction",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "node-0003",
      "name": "Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        240,
        -220
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Validate Transaction\n\nSingle Responsibility: gate the pipeline on shape/required-field checks mirroring transactionFormSchema (amount > 0, description present, type in enum, date parseable). Does not check for duplicates or resolve a category \u2014 those are separate stages. BudgetFlow's own API re-validates everything server-side regardless, so this is a fail-fast convenience, not the source of truth.\n\nInput: output of 02 - Processing / Parse Transaction.\nOutput (valid=true): passthrough + { valid: true, validationErrors: [] } \u2192 forwarded to Duplicate Check.\nOutput (valid=false): routes to 04 - Notifications / Import Failed and stops here.",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 560,
        "color": 4
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0002",
      "name": "On called",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflowTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        240,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "workflowInputs": {
          "values": []
        },
        "inputSource": "passthrough"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0004",
      "name": "Check Required Fields",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        520,
        300
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForAllItems",
        "jsCode": "const input = ($input.first() && $input.first().json) || {};\nconst errors = [];\n\nif (input.parseOk === false) {\n  errors.push(\"Parsing failed: \" + ((input.parseNotes || []).join(\"; \") || \"unknown reason\"));\n}\n\nconst amountNum = Number(input.amount);\nif (!input.amount || isNaN(amountNum) || amountNum <= 0) {\n  errors.push(\"Amount must be a number greater than zero.\");\n}\n\nif (!input.description || String(input.description).trim().length === 0) {\n  errors.push(\"Description is required.\");\n}\nif (input.description && String(input.description).length > 100) {\n  errors.push(\"Description cannot exceed 100 characters.\");\n}\n\nconst validTypes = [\"INCOME\", \"EXPENSE\", \"SAVINGS\", \"DEBT_PAYMENT\", \"TRANSFER\", \"REMITTANCE\"];\nif (!validTypes.includes(input.type)) {\n  errors.push(`Type must be one of: ${validTypes.join(\", \")}`);\n}\n\nconst parsedDate = input.date ? new Date(input.date) : null;\nif (!parsedDate || isNaN(parsedDate.getTime())) {\n  errors.push(\"Date is invalid.\");\n}\n\nreturn [{\n  json: {\n    ...input,\n    valid: errors.length === 0,\n    validationErrors: errors,\n  },\n}];"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "node-0005",
      "name": "Valid?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        800,
